[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1206484522","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1550#issuecomment-1206484522","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1550","id":1206484522,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85H6X4q","user":{"login":"swinslow","id":678569,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3ODU2OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/678569?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow","html_url":"https://github.com/swinslow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-08-05T13:53:54Z","updated_at":"2022-08-05T13:54:49Z","body":"Thanks for submitting this @zvr!\r\n\r\nI was involved with the development of this license while I was at the LF, so I'm going to refrain from being a +1 or -1 on adding this. Writing here to provide some additional context:\r\n\r\nThis license was developed by the [Academy Software Foundation (ASWF)](https://www.aswf.io) community. All of the software that ASWF develops is [open source](https://github.com/AcademySoftwareFoundation).\r\n\r\nThe Digital Assets License submitted here was developed to be used not for software, but rather for publicly sharing motion picture assets, such as extremely large data sets for 3D modeling. The license was intentionally drafted to permit broad redistribution, modification and use, but _not_ for all production purposes, rather for the subset of purposes listed in the license grant language at the top. In this way I wouldn't expect that it meets the full \"open content\" requirements for most such definitions, but may be appropriate to add on the basis of the other inclusion principles.\r\n\r\nThere's a blog post [here](https://linuxfoundation.org/blog/academy-software-foundation-giving-open-communities-access-to-production-grade-digital-assets-for-testing-demonstration-and-education-purposes/) which gives some more details on the context.\r\n\r\n_edited just after submitting to further clarify that this license was developed just for data sets / digital content, not for software_","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1206484522/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1212144962","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1550#issuecomment-1212144962","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1550","id":1212144962,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85IP91C","user":{"login":"jlovejoy","id":5048659,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNDg2NTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5048659?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy","html_url":"https://github.com/jlovejoy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-08-11T15:27:14Z","updated_at":"2022-08-31T04:48:58Z","body":"# New submission review\r\n\r\n## Has the license been approved by the OSI?\r\ndoes not seem so\r\n\r\n## Definitive factors\r\n*These must all be satisfied to allow inclusion in the license list*\r\n\r\n### Is the submitted license unique, that is, it does not match another license already on the License List as per the matching guidelines?\r\nit is unique\r\n\r\n### If a software license, does it apply to source code and not only to executables?\r\nmore of a content or data license than for software\r\n\r\n### Does the license have identifiable and stable text, and is not in the midst of drafting?\r\nyes, seems stable\r\n\r\n### Has the license steward, if any, committed to versioning new versions in the future and to not modify it after addition to the list?\r\nyes\r\n\r\n## Other factors for inclusion\r\n\r\n### 1. Does the license substantially comply with one of the free/open content definitions?\r\nNot entirely for two reasons:\r\n1) field of use restriction in first part, \"solely for education, training, research, software and hardware development, performance benchmarking (including publication of benchmark results and permitting reproducibility of the benchmark results by third parties), or software and hardware product demonstrations, are permitted provided that the following conditions are met\"\r\n\r\n2) The requirement to use a specific name in clause 4 has been historically been seen by some to be a restriction and therefore make a license non-free, but for our purposes here, I don't think that is grounds for exclusion.\r\n\r\n### 2. Is the license structured to be generally usable by anyone, and not specific to one organisation or project?\r\nyes\r\n\r\n### 3. Does the license have substantial use such that it is likely to be encountered (ie. use in many projects, or in one significant project)?\r\nI'm unclear as to actual use\r\n\r\n### 4. Is the license primarily intended to facilitate the free distribution of content with limited restrictions?\r\nI'd say this is mostly true - there are field of use restrictions as noted above, but it still allows a wide range of uses. It's interesting that it's drafted to list what IS allowed, rather than what is NOT allowed. This leaves some room for interpretation, but it's kind of like a commercial restriction in form.\r\n\r\n### 5. Does the license steward support this submission, or is at least aware of and not in opposition of it?\r\nyes\r\n\r\n## Summary of factors / outcome\r\nI'm leaning in favor of addition, pending some examples of actual use","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1212144962/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1212346561","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1550#issuecomment-1212346561","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1550","id":1212346561,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85IQvDB","user":{"login":"swinslow","id":678569,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3ODU2OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/678569?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow","html_url":"https://github.com/swinslow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-08-11T18:27:14Z","updated_at":"2022-08-11T18:27:14Z","body":"@jlovejoy Thanks -- on the review, I feel like I should note that the license grant language in the preamble is limited to only certain permitted uses. That may affect your view on the first \"other factor\".","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1212346561/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1216165364","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1550#issuecomment-1216165364","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1550","id":1216165364,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85IfTX0","user":{"login":"jlovejoy","id":5048659,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNDg2NTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5048659?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy","html_url":"https://github.com/jlovejoy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-08-16T05:29:03Z","updated_at":"2022-08-16T05:29:03Z","body":"thanks @swinslow - I somehow read that initially and then \"skipped\" it when I re-read and did the review!\r\n\r\nHere's a do-over on a couple of the factors:\r\n\r\n1. Does the license substantially comply with one of the free/open content definitions?\r\nNot really due to the usage restriction to \"solely for education, training, research, software and hardware development, performance benchmarking (including publication of benchmark results and permitting reproducibility of the benchmark results by third parties), or software and hardware product demonstrations, . . .\"\r\n\r\nAlso, the requirement to use a specific name in clause 4 has been historically been seen by some to be a restriction and therefore make a license non-free, but for our purposes here, I don't think that is grounds for exclusion.\r\n\r\n4. Is the license primarily intended to facilitate the free distribution of content with limited restrictions?\r\nI'd still say yes, as the allowable \"solely for\" uses cover a range of uses\r\n\r\nstill need more info as actual use (#3) - @zvr - do you have any insight as to that?","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1216165364/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1222469274","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1550#issuecomment-1222469274","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/li